<% content_for :title, "FAQ · LionDen" %>
<% content_for :hide_chrome, true %>

<div class="public_shell">
  <%= render "shared/public_nav" %>

  <main class="info_page">
    <h1 class="info_title">FAQ</h1>

    <div class="faq_item">
      <h2>Q: What is LionDen?</h2>
      <p>
        A: LionDen is one centralized “bulletin board” for student life. This application is authenticated:
        students must log in with their Columbia/Barnard email addresses to verify their student status.
        Students can then write posts or messages, either anonymously or under their name, about anything.
        They can assign these posts to one of many categories: Social, Academics, Housing, Buy/Sell Items,
        Travel, Help, etc.
      </p>
      <p>
        Users can “follow” a specific category that they are interested in, and can get notifications whenever
        a post is made in that category (email or text notifications). Anyone can reply to a post with a direct
        message, and the person who posted it will get the notification. This application will automatically
        create a group chat/messaging channel for all those who respond to a specific activity, and authors can
        set a limit on the number of people they are looking for.
      </p>
      <p>
        LionDen also facilitates meetups or informal, one-time/recurring gatherings like book clubs, movie nights,
        or group concert trips. This kind of “meetup” can be a posted event with a description, date, time, and
        location. Students can join once or on a recurring basis, and these events will appear on an integrated
        calendar where they can see all the events for the week/month. You can see a calendar for all general
        events, as well as one with the specific events you signed up for.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="faq_item">
      <h2>Q: Who can join?</h2>
      <p>A: Only students with a @columbia.edu or @barnard.edu Google account, so you know you're talking to a verified student.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="faq_item">
      <h2>Q: Can I post anonymously?</h2>
      <p>A: Yes. Any post or reply can be anonymous or display your name.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="faq_item">
      <h2>Q: Why do posts expire?</h2>
      <p>A: Authors choose when their posts disappear (for example, "tonight", "this week", or a custom time), so the board only shows relevant and current events.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="faq_item">
      <h2>Q: Is this an official Columbia app?</h2>
      <p>A: No. LionDen is a student project and isn't affiliated with Columbia University.</p>
    </div>
  </main>
</div>